Link with \fI-lexpanse\fR.
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBexpanse_ordered_bytesmap_t\fR is an ordered dynamic radix trie mapping
arbitrary byte strings (\fBconst void *\fR, with explicit \fBsize_t len\fR)
to 64-bit integer values (\fBuint64_t\fR). Unlike \fBexpanse_strmap_t\fR,
keys may contain embedded NUL bytes (\fB0x00\fR) and arbitrary binary data.
Keys are ordered lexicographically.
.PP
Navigation functions accept caller-allocated destination buffers
(\fBkey_out\fR and \fBbuf_len\fR) and return an
\fBexpanse_ordered_bytes_nav_status\fR enum:
.TP
.B EXPANSE_ORDERED_BYTES_NAV_OK (0)
A matching entry was found and its decoded key was written to
\fBkey_out\fR. If non-null, \fB*required_len\fR receives the key length
and \fB*value_out\fR receives the value.
.TP
.B EXPANSE_ORDERED_BYTES_NAV_NOT_FOUND (1)
No matching key exists in the map.
.TP
.B EXPANSE_ORDERED_BYTES_NAV_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL (2)
A matching entry exists, but \fBbuf_len\fR is insufficient (or \fBkey_out\fR
is NULL). No bytes are written to \fBkey_out\fR and \fBvalue_out\fR is
untouched. If non-null, \fB*required_len\fR is populated with the exact
buffer size needed to hold the key. Passing \fBkey_out == NULL\fR and
\fBbuf_len == 0\fR allows probing the required length.
.SS Held Memory
.TP
.BI "size_t expanse_ordered_bytesmap_mem_held("
.BI "    const expanse_ordered_bytesmap_t *" map ");"
Returns the heap bytes the map holds from the system allocator:
\fBexpanse_ordered_bytesmap_mem_used\fR() plus freed blocks retained.
.TP
.BI "size_t expanse_ordered_bytesmap_shrink_to_fit("
.BI "    expanse_ordered_bytesmap_t *" map ");"
Releases retained memory after deletions to the system allocator and
returns the bytes released.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <inttypes.h>
#include <expanse.h>

int main(void) {
    expanse_ordered_bytesmap_t *map = expanse_ordered_bytesmap_new();

    const char key1[] = "hello\\0world";
    expanse_ordered_bytesmap_insert(map, key1, sizeof(key1) - 1, 42, NULL);

    /* Point query */
    uint64_t val;
    if (expanse_ordered_bytesmap_get(map, key1, sizeof(key1) - 1, &val)) {
        printf("found: %" PRIu64 "\\n", val);
    }

    /* Probe required length, then fetch */
    size_t req = 0;
    expanse_ordered_bytes_nav_status st;
    st = expanse_ordered_bytesmap_first(map, NULL, 0, &req, NULL);
    if (st == EXPANSE_ORDERED_BYTES_NAV_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL) {
        char buf[256];
        if (req <= sizeof(buf)) {
            st = expanse_ordered_bytesmap_first(
                map, buf, sizeof(buf), &req, &val
            );
            if (st == EXPANSE_ORDERED_BYTES_NAV_OK) {
                printf("first key len: %zu, val: %" PRIu64 "\\n", req, val);
            }
        }
    }

    expanse_ordered_bytesmap_free(map);
    return 0;
}
.fi
.SS Example Output
.nf
found: 42
first key len: 11, val: 42
.fi
